course: dictionary
lesson: 6655
title: Nurse: a word with more than one job
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: A nurse is a person trained to look after sick or injured people. Read the sentence «In hospital you can ask questions and tell the nurses how you feel, because they are there to help you.» The clue is «help you»: a nurse is someone whose job is to help people who are not well.
explain: Nurse can also be a doing word. «Nurse someone back to health» means to take care of them until they get better. Nurse is a noun in one sentence and a verb in another, so look at the words around it to see which job it does.
explain: Nurse can also mean feeding a baby with milk, or keeping a feeling for a long time, as in «nurse a grudge». The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning fits: a baby, a hurt, a sick person, or a bad feeling. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A nurse is a person trained to look after sick or injured people.
fact: Nurses usually work in hospitals, clinics or schools.
fact: The school nurse checks injuries, hearing and eyesight.
fact: To nurse someone means to take care of them when they are ill.
fact: A nursery is a place for babies or young children, or a place for growing plants. It shares its word with nurse.
exercise: «Lily stays with Chloe in the nurse's room after Chloe's plaits are pulled so hard she cries.» What is the nurse's room? | A room where hair is cut | A room for storing plaits | A classroom for maths | *A room where a helper looks after children who are hurt or upset
exercise: «The nurse checked my ear and said it was fine.» What job does a nurse do here? | *Looks after people who are sick or injured | Drives the school bus | Teaches maths in class | Sells food in the canteen
exercise: Mum says, «I will nurse you back to health.» What does nurse mean here? | Write a letter to the doctor | *Take care of someone until they get better | Feed a baby with milk | Hold a feeling for a long time
test: «Before a vaccination (often called a «jab») you can tell the nurse you are scared.» What does the word «jab» mean? | A sweet from the shop | A hospital bed on wheels | A kind of plaster | *A small injection that protects you from illness
test: Which word means a place for babies or young children? | nursing | nurse | *nursery | nursed
exam: «Dad sat by the bed all night to nurse his sick brother.» What does nurse mean in this sentence? | To work in a hospital clinic | To feed a baby with milk | To hold a grudge for a long time | *To take care of someone who is ill
